<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korea's AFMC buys 55,000 T of US soybeans.</title>
<headline>South Korea's AFMC buys 55,000 T of US soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural and Fishery Marketing Corp (AFMC) said on Thursday it bought a total of 55,000 tonnes of U.S. No. 1 soybeans from Cargill and Daewoo.  </p>
<p>An official at the AFMC said arrival for 30,000 tonnes is slated for January 30 and for 25,000 slated for February 20 to the Western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>Details are as follows: Position    Tonne    Shipment		 Price-Seller Tonne Cnf</p>
<p>			 U.S. Gulf, U.S. PNW</p>
<p>one	  30,000  Dec 6-25   Dec 21-Jan 10     $309.58 Daewoo</p>
<p>two	  25,000  Dec 26-Jan 15 Jan 11-30	$302.99 Cargill</p>
</text>
